I've implemented a patch[1] for this, along with a couple of
variations. Different molds can be used in fruit juice to make
different potions (nothing magical, just 'natural medicenes').

To make it interesting, the process is _not_ instantaneous. You
dissolve the mold in the juice and then 50-100 turns later it changes.
This means there's a bit of complexity with splitting and merging
groups of fermenting potions, but I think I've sorted it out. The only
probably is that it is too hard to detect the case where two fermenting
potions can be merged, so if you start two together then drop one and
pick it back up, it won't with the other.

My only concern about this patch is that it may give you a way to brew
smoky or milky potions, depending on the colour of booze (and the other
products). I think the sensible solution would be to set a flag on the
potion which indicates that it can never be inhabited.

